Syntax: rites <corpse>

Rites draws what is left of a soul out of a body and puts it into a
soulstone, where it waits to be spent on armor.

You must be seated, holding your holy symbol, with holy water to hand and a
soulstone to catch what comes.  The body must be whole: skinned, butchered
or dissected, it has already been opened and there is nothing left to call.

What a stone takes is its own level against a tenth of the corpse's, so a
deep stone takes more from the same body.  Your own level never enters it,
and your skill decides only whether the words land, never how much they
yield.

A body the rites have been said over is finished.  Nothing else can be taken
from it, and it cannot be sacrificed.

See also: ENSOUL, BOLSTER, SOULSTONE
